WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:08.967
<v Rohan>My pencil is six point four centimetres... no, six point zero! It keeps changing!

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:13.552
<v Mishu>Your eye is moving, not the pencil! Look from straight above the mark.

00:00:13.452 --> 00:00:16.399
<v Mishu>Looking from the side gives a parallax error.

00:00:16.399 --> 00:00:18.769
<v Ishita>Six point two. Every time!

00:00:18.769 --> 00:00:27.441
<v Mishu>Long ago, the standard metre was the gap between two fine marks on a metal bar in Paris, and exact copies went all over the world.

00:00:27.441 --> 00:00:32.081
<v Rohan>And for long trips, we climb the ladder: a thousand metres make a kilometre!

00:00:32.081 --> 00:00:35.911
<v Ishita>But how do I measure something really thin, like one coin?

00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:41.934
<v Mishu>Stack ten coins, measure the stack, and divide by ten. Measure many, then divide!
